---
title: Proposition 17
---
order: 17
---
short_label: I.17
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In any triangle the sum of any two angles is less than two right angles.
----
proof:

Let {ABC} be a triangle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="260" height="210" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="I.17 diagram" src="propI17.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "I.17",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;80,30",
            "B;point;free;30,180",
            "C;point;free;140,180",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random",
            // BC produced to D (the exterior angle at C). CD is the
            // produced part; the triangle polygon draws BC itself.
            "D;point;lineSlider;B,C,220,180",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            // Zero-color hover target for the side BC.
            "BC;line;connect;B,C;0;0;0",
            // Angle markers. The angle at B is named CBA (the triangle
            // owns "ABC"); "the angle ABC" in prose uses {ABC|CBA}. At C,
            // ACB (interior) and ACD (exterior) are adjacent — #103 nests.
            "ACD;sector;angleMarker;C,A,D",
            "ACB;sector;angleMarker;C,A,B",
            "CBA;sector;angleMarker;B,C,A",
            "BAC;sector;angleMarker;A,B,C"
        ],
        // D (BC produced) is constructed mid-proof.
        deferDraggables: ["D"],
