              },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.2" }] },
            { text: "Since the angle {ACD} is an exterior angle of the triangle {ABC}, therefore it is greater than the interior and opposite angle {ABC|CBA}. Add the angle {ACB} to each. Then the sum of the angles {ACD} and {ACB} is greater than the sum of the angles {ABC|CBA} and {BCA}.",
              visible: ["ABC","CBA","ACB","BAC","D","CD","ACD"],
              highlighted: ["ACD","CBA","ACB"],
              transition: {
                  animations: [
                      { elem: "ACD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep }
                  ]
              },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.16" }, { ref: "C.N." }] },
            { text: "But the sum of the angles {ACD} and {ACB} is equal to two right angles. Therefore the sum of the angles {ABC|CBA} and {BCA} is less than two right angles.",
